[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ This is a very basic opening that is good for starters and sometimes used by Grandmasters. Move to the most common square e4. }
1. e4 { Black retaliates. } 1... e5 { Move Knf3 } { [%csl Gg1] } 2. Nf3 { This move makes the e5 pawn weak. And also it develops a knight that also fights for the center. } { [%csl Bf3,Re5,Ye4,Yd4,Yd5][%cal Bf3e5,Bf3d4] } 2... Nc6 { Black fights back while defends the e5 pawn from the f3 knight. Move Bc4 } 3. Bc4 { This is the Italian opening! This move targets the f7 weak pawn. TIP: If you want, you can take that pawn, for a positional advantage because now black can’t castle, and Knf5 can check the king early } { [%csl Rc4,Rg5,Gg1][%cal Rc4f7,Ge8f7,Rf3g5,Rg5f7,Ge1g1,Gh1f1,Gb1c3] } *


