{ This Opening is also good for beginners. It is very simple and easy to learn! Move to e4. }
1. e4 { Black fights back. } 1... e5 { Remember, Always try to take control of the the center, or change it into a death trap. (Chapter 6) By moving to Nf3, we take control. } { [%csl Yd5,Yd4,Ye4,Ye5,Gg1][%cal Gg1f3] } 2. Nf3 Nc6 { This is like the Italian opening, The two knights are fighting for the pawns. move to d4. } { [%csl Bf3,Bc6,Gd2] } 3. d4 { This move pressures the pawn of e5. If accepted, you simply take with Knxd4. With the queen defending this is a win for the center so far. This opening is also good for Beginners. } { [%csl Bf3,Bd1,Rc6,Re5][%cal Bd1d4,Bf3d4] } *


