{ The Sicilian Defense is one of the most solid defenses in chess. }
1. e4 { Move to c5 } 1... c5 { This blocks the move d4 to try to role the center. Much like the Dutch opening. } { [%csl Bc5][%cal Bc5d4,Bc7c5] } 2. Nf3 { Move to d6 } 2... d6 { This stakes claim with the square e5 and takes control over the center. } 3. d4 { The c4 pawn is getting pressured. Do cxd4 } { [%cal Rd1d4,Rf3d4] } 3... cxd4 { Nice } 4. Nxd4 { How can you put pressure on the e4 pawn? } { [%csl Re4,Bg8] } 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 { This is the Sicilian Defense. There are many variations, such as the dragon (Green), or the Najdorf (Red) which puts white in uncomfortable positions. } { [%csl Gf7,Gg6,Gh7][%cal Rb7b5,Ra7a6,Re7e5,Rf8e7,Rc8e6,Rd8c7,Rb8c6,Gf8g7,Gg7g6,Ge8g8,Gh8f8] } *


